      "side": 1,
      "message": "Oh, looks like I misunderstood it a little. It looks like `\\n` is emitted into the ninja file as a newline, but soong recognizes it and inserts a `$` before it to escape it from ninja. So you get a ninja file like:\n\n\n```\nrule m.cole_test_android_common.bootconfig.txt\n    command \u003d rm -f out/soong/.intermediates/build/soong/cole_test/android_common/cole_test/bootconfig.txt \u0026\u0026 echo  foo$\n  \u003e\u003e  out/soong/.intermediates/build/soong/cole_test/android_common/cole_test/bootconfig.txt \u0026\u0026 echo  bar$\n  \u003e\u003e  out/soong/.intermediates/build/soong/cole_test/android_common/cole_test/bootconfig.txt \u0026\u0026 echo  baz$\n  \u003e\u003e  out/soong/.intermediates/build/soong/cole_test/android_common/cole_test/bootconfig.txt # hash of input list: e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855\n```\n\nSo I guess the `\\n` wasn\u0027t doing any harm, but also wasn\u0027t necessary.",
